--- a function handed as a value types the parameter by what it answers
--- once the functions it calls are copied: `next_of` calls `wrap`'s copy
--- for ints, and the parameter had kept an earlier round's guess — the
--- list of text `wrap`'s other copy answers — so the compiled call did not
--- build (Rosetta Code, Monads/List monad)

fn wrap[x]
    return [x]

fn applied[x, f]
    return f[x]

fn next_of[x]
    return wrap[x + 1]

log[applied[1, next_of]]
log[wrap['a']]
